      "agent": "Reviewer",
      "note": "CROSS-CUTTING SCHEMA DEBT (surfaced in WP-004, impacts all downstream WPs): movies_filenames.hash has a UNIQUE constraint in the live spdb_tests database that is NOT present in the structure.sql reference file. The structure.sql was generated without ALTER TABLE...ADD UNIQUE statements. Any downstream WP that inserts rows into movies_filenames (e.g. LibraryScanner, DapperMovieCatalogRepository) MUST use INSERT IGNORE or ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE to avoid MySqlException on duplicate hash. The Developer flagged this in the WP-004 implementation pipeline. Action required: (1) update structure.sql to reflect the live schema, and (2) ensure all INSERT statements for movies_filenames use duplicate-safe syntax."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "priority": "high",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-07T21:19:27Z",
      "agent": "Documentation",
      "note": "CRITICAL DEBT — surfaced by WP-004 Developer: movies_filenames.hash has a UNIQUE constraint in the live spdb_tests schema that is NOT visible in structure.sql (the reference SQL file was generated without the corresponding ALTER TABLE...ADD UNIQUE statement). The spec implies a one-to-many relationship (many filenames per hash) but the live schema enforces one-to-one (one filename per hash). All downstream WPs that INSERT into movies_filenames (e.g. WP-005 LibraryScanner, DapperMovieCatalogRepository) MUST use INSERT IGNORE or ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE to avoid MySqlException on duplicate hash inserts. Confirmed by QA and Security Auditor during WP-004 pipeline. Reviewer forwarded to Documentation for project-level visibility."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "priority": "high",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-08T09:06:15Z",
      "agent": "Synthesis",
      "note": "SYNTHESIS CROSS-CUTTING OBSERVATION: Three recurring patterns across M3 WPs warrant systematic M4 action. (1) SCHEMA DEBT: structure.sql does not reflect the live UNIQUE constraint on movies_filenames.hash — all downstream WPs that wrote to movies_filenames worked around this by using INSERT IGNORE, which is correct, but the reference file must be updated before any future developer relies on it for schema setup. (2) TEST ISOLATION: Multiple live-DB test classes share the MySQL movies table without serialisation; ER_CHECKREAD races appear under parallel test runs because the movies table appears to use MyISAM (no MVCC). Add [Collection(\\\"LiveDB\\\")] and verify table engine before M4 CI integration. (3) EVENT SUBSCRIPTION LEAKS: RefreshIndexViewModel and MainContentViewModel subscribe to IRefreshOrchestrator.StateChanged without unsubscribing (no IDisposable). Harmless for singleton-lifetime VMs today, but a structural risk if VM lifetimes change in M4+."
    }
